  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Diego is walking home from school at a constant rate. This graph represents function \(d\), which gives his distance from home, in kilometers, \(m\) minutes since leaving the school.</para>
<para>Use the graph to find or estimate:</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Graph of line. Horizontal axis, 0 to 24 by 4’s, minutes since leaving school. Vertical axis, 0 to 3 by point 5’s, kilometers from home. Line starts at about 0 comma 2 point 2 5, and ends at 20 comma 0."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/e1edaa833b2861d34842791bee74f5475acd6954"/></media></figure></para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is \(d(0)\), and what does it represent in the situation?
        Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <para>\(d(0)=2.25\); Zero minutes after Diego has left school, he is 2.25 kilometers from home, or Diego’s school is a little more than 2 kilometers from his house.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(d(12) =\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <para>\(d(12)=0.9\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What does \(d(m)=1\) mean in the context of the problem, and what is \(m\)?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <para>\(m\) is approximately 10.5. After approximately 10.5 minutes, Diego is 1 kilometer from home.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What does \(d(m)=0\) mean in the context of the problem, and what is \(m\)?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <para>\(m\) is 20. After 20 minutes, Diego is 0 kilometers from home, or it takes Diego 20 minutes to walk the 2.25 kilometers home from school.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
